            <ArticleTitle>HelpDesk answers: is it safe to add long-acting β-2 agonists to inhaled corticosteroids in patients with persistent asthma?</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>370-1</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Possibly. Long-acting β-2 agonists (LABAs) used in combination with inhaled corticosteroids (ICS) don't appear to increase all-cause mortality or serious adverse events in patients with persistent asthma compared with ICS alone. Studies showing an increase in catastrophic events had serious methodologic issues. A large surveillance study is ongoing.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
